# Research: large raw per-run dumps that `research/<slug>/run.py` rewrites and no README links
# to. The summary files that the READMEs cite (summary.json, q*.json, ...) stay committed.
research/regularized-newton-arc/results/runs_convex.json
research/regularized-newton-arc/results/runs_nonconvex.json
research/clenshaw-curtis-vs-gauss/results/error_curves.json

# Research: `run.py` writes every figure as .svg and .png; git keeps only the format that the
# READMEs show (SVG when it is at most ~300 KB, else PNG). Run `research/shrink_figures.py` on the
# kept figures before you commit them.
research/anderson-acceleration/figures/*.png
research/pdlp-restarted-pdhg/figures/*.png
research/restarted-accelerated-gradient/figures/*.png
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/convergence.png
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/performance_profiles.png
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/sensitivity.png
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/outcome_maps_convex.svg
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/outcome_maps_nonconvex.svg
research/regularized-newton-arc/figures/saddle_paths.svg
